From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmony.io>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 18:09:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix -Wunused-function warning with clang on HarmonyOS

Clang on HarmonyOS enforces -Wunused-function even for static inline
functions, unlike gcc. The print_sigmask_addr_size function in
src/sigreturn.c may be unused on certain architectures (e.g., aarch64
uses arch_sigreturn.c with print_sigset_addr instead of
tprintsigmask_addr), causing the build to fail with -Werror.

Add __attribute__((unused)) guarded by __OHOS__ to suppress the
warning only on HarmonyOS, preserving upstream's design intent for
other platforms.
---
 src/sigreturn.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sigreturn.c b/src/sigreturn.c
--- a/src/sigreturn.c
+++ b/src/sigreturn.c
@@ -16,7 +16,16 @@ typedef struct {
 #endif
 
 /* The following function might be unused, hence the inline qualifier.  */
+#ifdef __OHOS__
+/*
+ * Clang on HarmonyOS enforces -Wunused-function even for static inline
+ * functions, unlike gcc. Add __attribute__((unused)) to suppress the
+ * warning when building on HarmonyOS.
+ */
+static inline __attribute__((unused)) void
+#else
 static inline void
+#endif
 print_sigmask_addr_size(const void *const addr, const unsigned int size)
 {
 	tprint_struct_begin();
-- 
